  "verbalization": "Leuconodine E appears to have a complex target network that ultimately leads to Tankyrase-2 through multiple intermediate entities. The evidence suggests that leuconodine E directly targets Raji, which in turn is targeted by several compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and (1R,4S,5R,8R,10S,13R,14R,16R,19S,20S)-10,16,19-trihydroxy-4,5,9,9,13,19,20-heptamethyl-21-oxahexacyclo[18.2.2.01,18.04,17.05,14.08,13]tetracos-17-en-22-one. All of these intermediates share a common relationship with Tankyrase-2, indicating a potential pathway through which leuconodine E may exert its effects. The integration of these evidence points suggests that leuconodine E may act through a mechanism that involves targeting Raji, which in turn influences Tankyrase-2 via a series of molecular interactions. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between leuconodine E and Tankyrase-2, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
